Day 10 — GCP DevOps CI/CD (Cloud Build + Artifact Registry + GitOps)

Scenario-Based DevOps Interview Questions

1️⃣ Your team wants a fully automated CI/CD pipeline for containerized apps. How will you design it using Cloud Build + Artifact Registry + GKE/Cloud Run?

2️⃣ Builds are taking too long due to repetitive tasks (dependency download, image build). What Cloud Build optimizations will you implement?

3️⃣ You need to enforce security scans (SAST, container vulnerability scanning) before deployment. How will you integrate this in Cloud Build?

4️⃣ A pipeline must deploy to dev → stage → prod with approval gates. How will you design this flow in Cloud Build + Cloud Deploy?

5️⃣ You need GitOps-style delivery for GKE clusters. Which tools will you use (Config Sync, Anthos Config Management, ArgoCD) and why?

6️⃣ A Cloud Build service account is over-permissioned. How will you apply least privilege for building, pushing images, and deploying?

7️⃣ You must build multi-architecture container images (AMD64 + ARM). How will you modify the pipeline?

8️⃣ A deployment to GKE failed with a permissions error and kubeconfig mismatch. How will you debug and fix Cloud Build → GKE authentication?

9️⃣ You want to implement policy-as-code (security checks, naming conventions, labels) before deployment. Which tools and services will you choose?

🔟 Artifacts in Artifact Registry are growing uncontrollably. How will you manage cleanup, retention policies, and repository design?

1️⃣1️⃣ You must integrate Terraform into Cloud Build for infra deployment. How will you manage state files, secrets, and environment segregation?

1️⃣2️⃣ A Cloud Run service must be deployed automatically on every commit but with traffic-splitting rollout. How will you implement this?

1️⃣3️⃣ Deployment to prod should only be allowed during specific maintenance windows. How will you enforce time-based policy in CI/CD?

1️⃣4️⃣ You need detailed logs, metrics, and traceability for every pipeline step. What Cloud Build & Cloud Logging features will you enable?

1️⃣5️⃣ You must create a DR-ready CI/CD pipeline where artifacts, configs, and environments exist in multiple regions. How will you design failover for CI/CD?

